<title>GERMANY: Berlusconi says Kohl affirms EMU goals, timetable.</title>
<headline>Berlusconi says Kohl affirms EMU goals, timetable.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian opposition leader Silvio Berlusconi said on Thursday after meeting German Chancellor Helmut Kohl the German leader had told him the timetable and criteria for European monetary union would be adhered to.</p>
<p>&quot;The chancellor reconfirmed that the drive for European union continues. The Maastricht Treaty will be adhered to in terms of meeting the criteria and the timetable,&quot; Berlusconi told a news conference.</p>
<p>Berlusconi, a former Italian prime minister, said Kohl appeared as committed as ever to the cause of European integration. </p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
</text>
